      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Marigold V2 -- Marigold V2 - surface normals\n\nPer-pixel **surface normals** from a single photo. Ground faces up (green), surfaces facing the camera are lilac.\n\nMarigold V2 (SIGGRAPH Asia 2026) turns **Qwen-Image-Edit-2509** into a dense\npredictor with a small LoRA, and runs it as **one deterministic step** -- no\nnoise, no CFG, no text encoder. The prompt is a fixed tensor loaded from\n`models/embeddings` by **Load Conditioning**.\n\n## What this graph needs\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| UNET | `qwen_image_edit_2509_fp8_e4m3fn.safetensors` (any Qwen-Image-Edit-2509 build works -- Marigold is a LoRA over it) |\n| LoRA | `marigold_v2\\marigold_v2_normals.safetensors` |\n| VAE | `marigold_v2\\marigold_v2_normals_vae.safetensors` |\n| conditioning | `marigold_v2\\marigold_v2_normals_conditioning.safetensors` |\n\nAll from https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/marigold-v2-0 except the base UNET,\nwhich was already on this drive. Requires **ComfyUI 0.35.0+** for\n`MarigoldV2PostProcess`, `ConditioningLoader` and the `img_to_img_velocity`\nsampling mode -- no custom nodes.\n\n## Three things that are easy to get wrong\n\n1. **The Marigold VAE does the encode as well as the decode.** It is a\n   task-specific VAE, not the stock `qwen_image_vae`; both VAEEncode and\n   VAEDecode use it.\n2. **`ModelSamplingAuraFlow` must be set to `img_to_img_velocity`.** On the\n   default `flow` setting the prediction is wrong, not merely worse.\n3. **Sigmas are `0.5, 0` with noise disabled.** That is the single\n   deterministic step. There is no seed and no sampler randomness.\n\n## Resolution\n\nThe `ImageScaleToTotalPixels` node caps the input at 1 MP. Qwen-Image-Edit\nworks at about that size; a 4160x6240 photo fed in raw took **340 s** against\n**6 s** at 1 MP, for the same quality. Raise `megapixels` if you need more\ndetail, and expect the cost to scale with pixels.\n\nSwap the task by changing the LoRA, the VAE, the conditioning and the\nPost-Process `prediction` dropdown together -- all four must agree. A third\nset (`albedo`) is on the drive if you want it; its LoRA and VAE are not\ndownloaded yet.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
